# R5 risky surfaces for claude-code-fleet-notify — a PR touching ANY of these
# requires both adversarial auditors (audit/grok + audit/gatekeeper) to post a
# success commit status before it can merge (enforced by r5-audit-gate.yml).
#
# DESIGN: broad default-covering GLOBS, not a drift-prone allowlist (the
# orchestrator's allowlist omitted real buggy files — same lesson here).
# Over-gate trivial changes for safety > under-gate a fleet-wide-blast surface.
#
# The hook layer — a bad hook command disabled every tool on the machine once
# (the 2026-06-11 outage class); changes here drive every session:
hooks/*.py
# The delivery library (inbox/daemon/handoff/trace):
notifications/*.py
# The installer (wires the hooks; the outage came through here) + daemon + deploy:
scripts/install-hooks.sh
scripts/start_notify_daemons.sh
scripts/atomic_deploy.sh
scripts/_stage_b_api.py
# CI / gate config itself (self-protecting):
.github/workflows/*.yml
.github/r5-risky-paths
# Packaging:
setup.py
